ginal close to the Laplace value on the 3-animal fixture; `fit_laplace_reml(...; family = :beta_binomial, n_trials, rho)` estimates `sigma_a2` (Brent) at a SUPPLIED FIXED ρ (both keywords required; `marginal = :variational` rejected), and `nongaussian_result_payload` self-describes the fit with `family = "beta_binomial"` and the fixed ρ in a new `dispersion` field. An opt-in seeded recovery harness (`sim/phase6_betabinomial_recovery.jl`, outside CI; checkpoint `docs/dev-log/recovery-checkpoints/2026-06-22-h2-betabinomial-recovery.md`) on 5 pre-declared seeds (q = 345, m = 20, ρ = 0.2 supplied at truth) passes the hard gate 5/5 (converged ∧ interior σ̂²a ∧ EBV cor 0.74–0.82) and the σ̂²a magnitude recovered well (mean 0.949 vs 1.0, mean rel 0.153, 5/5 within rel ≤ 0.45 reported-not-gated) — m = 20 makes the overdispersed fit informative, conditional on a correctly supplied ρ. Still needs joint `(sigma_a2, ρ)` estimation, a VA/ELBO kernel, a per-record `BetaBinomialVectorResponse`, a `sigma_a2` profile interval (H6), an external comparator (MCMCglmm/aods3/glmmTMB), latent-scale h², and an R `beta_binomial()` formula/bridge activation; INTERNAL (not exported), not the public default, not covered |
