 | V6-GGLLVM-DESC | Genetic-GLLVM latent-structure descriptors + Gaussian latent solve (supplied loadings) (Phase 6, #50 slices 1–2) | partial | `genetic_gllvm_descriptors(Λ; uniqueness)` reports the rotation-INVARIANT descriptors of a genetic-GLLVM latent layer from SUPPLIED `traits × K` loadings `Λ` (+ optional positive uniqueness `Ψ`): `genetic_covariance` `Σ_g = ΛΛ' (+ diag Ψ)`, `genetic_variances`, `genetic_correlation`, `communality` `c²_t = (ΛΛ')_tt / Σ_g[t,t]`, `genetic_pca`/`g_max`, and `rank`/`n_latent_factors = K` — a pure composition of `lowrank_covariance`/`factor_analytic_covariance`/`genetic_correlation` (`multivariate.jl`) and `genetic_pca`/`g_max` (`evolvability.jl`), no new estimation. Validated (`test/runtests.jl`, 24 deterministic RNG-free assertions): exact `Σ_g == lowrank_covariance(Λ)` (Ψ absent) and `== factor_analytic_covariance(Λ, Ψ)`; `communality == 1` at `Ψ = 0`, matches `(ΛΛ')_tt / Σ_g[t,t]` and is strictly in `(0,1)` with positive `Ψ`; the binding rotation-invariance gate (for orthogonal `Q`, `Λ → ΛQ` leaves `Σ_g`, `genetic_variances`, `communality`, `genetic_correlation`, and the `genetic_pca` eigenvalues invariant); the `K = t`, `Λ = I`, `Ψ = 0` reduction (`Σ_g = I`, communality 1, eigenvalues all 1); and delegated dimension/positivity/rank guards. DESCRIPTIVE, supplied-covariance only — `Λ`/`Ψ` NOT estimated, no marginal/likelihood/fit, no R model-spec or bridge payload, only rotation-invariant functionals (never raw loadings). Slice 2 adds the Gaussian latent solve `genetic_gllvm_gaussian_mme(Y, X, Z, Ainv, Λ, R0; uniqueness)`: since `Cov(vec(U)) = G_lat ⊗ A` under a Gaussian response, the Gaussian genetic GLLVM IS the multivariate animal model at `G0 = G_lat = ΛΛ'(+diag Ψ)`, so the function builds `G_lat` and delegates to `multivariate_mme`, returning that solve plus the rotation-invariant `latent_structure`. Validated (`test/runtests.jl`): the defining identity (`== multivariate_mme` at `G0 = G_lat`, exact β + EBVs), rotation inv