         "`BernoulliProbitResponse` (internal) extends the non-Gaussian engine to a BINARY threshold (liability-scale) animal model with the probit link `P(y=1) = Φ(η)`: an unobserved liability `η + e`, `e ~ N(0,1)`, is observed as `y = 1[liability > 0]`. With the sign trick `s = 2y−1`, the conditional is `ℓ = log Φ(sη)`, the score is the signed inverse-Mills ratio `s·φ(sη)/Φ(sη)`, and the IRLS weight is `M(sη)·(M(sη)+sη) ∈ (0,1)` — the probit conditional is LOG-CONCAVE, so its observed information is strictly positive and equals the expected information (no Fisher-scoring substitution is needed, in contrast to the beta-binomial). Dependency-free standard-normal primitives were added (`_norm_pdf`, `_norm_logpdf`, a tail-stable `_norm_logcdf`, and `_norm_mills`): `Φ`/`erfc` reuse the module's already-validated incomplete-gamma (`erfc(z) = Q(1/2, z²)`), and a LOG-form continued fraction keeps `_norm_logcdf` FINITE into the deep tail (`x = −40`); the coarse genomic `_standard_normal_cdf_approx` (7.5e-8) is intentionally NOT reused for the likelihood derivatives. Validated (`test/runtests.jl`): `Φ` matches standard values to 1e-12 (`Φ(0)=0.5`, `Φ(1.96)=0.97500210…`); `_norm_logcdf` stays finite at `x = −10/−20/−40` and `Φ(x)+Φ(−x)=1` across the tail; the log-form tail cf agrees with the package incomplete-gamma `Q`; the conditional score AND weight match central finite differences (rtol 1e-5); the weight is strictly positive across a `(y, η)` grid incl. the deep tail `η = −6`; the Laplace Newton mode is stationary (‖∇‖ < 1e-8); a β-fixed INDEPENDENT tensor Gauss–Hermite quadrature of the TRUE probit marginal is close to the Laplace value on the 3-animal fixture (binary gap documented, as for Bernoulli); `fit_laplace_reml(...; family = :bernoulli_probit)` estimates `sigma_a2` (Brent) and converges; `laplace_reml_interval(...; family = :bernoulli_probit)` returns the clamp-flagged single-component interval; `nongaussian_result_payload` carries `family = \"bernoulli_probit\"` with NO heritability field (liability scale) and `dispersion = nothing`; and a non-{0,1} response is guarded. LAPLACE ONLY — the probit variational expected information is response-dependent (`−E[ℓ″]` varies with `s = 2y−1`), which the response-free `_fam_expected_weight` signature cannot carry, so `marginal = :variational` is rejected (a VA kernel is explicit follow-up). An opt-in seeded recovery harness (`sim/phase6_threshold_recovery.jl`, outside CI; checkpoint `docs/dev-log/recovery-checkpoints/2026-06-22-threshold-recovery.md`) on 5 pre-declared seeds (q = 345, liability-threshold DGP) passes the hard gate 5/5 (converged ∧ interior σ̂²a ∧ EBV cor 0.61–0.76), with the σ̂²a MAGNITUDE is REPORTED-NOT-GATED (3/5 within rel ≤ 0.45; mean σ̂²a 0.633 vs 1.0); the five-seed sample mean is below truth but does not establish population bias or cause.",
