-        "COVERED (SCOPED, validation-scale, opt-in; NOT the public default — public-covered FITTING stays 1 = v0.1 Gaussian) via the doc-16 G11 substitutable gate, path (b): one same-estimand Laplace-ML comparator leg (`ordinal::clmm`) plus a passing pre-declared 48-seed recovery gate. \"Covered\" means the engine correctly implements ordered-probit JOINT estimation of σ²a + the K−1 cutpoints on an informative A=I/repeated-records design — NOT small-sample accuracy of σ²a (bias +0.027, 1.44·MCSE; read as no detectable bias, never \"unbiased\"). SCOPE OF VALIDITY: A=I/repeated-records single design (q=120×4=480 obs), Laplace-only, dense, asymptotic, INTERNAL. STANDING DEBT (covered does NOT retire it): broader-DGP + pedigree-A (non-I) recovery; a 2nd same-estimand comparator (MCMCglmm `threshold` is Bayesian-agreement-only and does NOT discharge the leg); the `:symbol` payload + scale-labelled observation-scale h²; and R activation. `OrderedProbitResponse(thresholds)` (internal) generalizes `BernoulliProbitResponse` to K ORDERED categories `1..K` on a standard-normal latent scale with `K-1` SUPPLIED, strictly-increasing cutpoints `θ`: with liability `l = η + e`, `e ~ N(0,1)`, `P(y=k|η) = Φ(θ_k−η) − Φ(θ_{k-1}−η)` (`θ_0=−∞`, `θ_K=+∞`). The conditional `ℓ = log P(y|η)` is LOG-CONCAVE in η (log of a Gaussian interval probability), so the score `(φ(θ_{k-1}−η) − φ(θ_k−η))/P` and the OBSERVED-information IRLS weight `score² − (a·φ(a) − b·φ(b))/P` are exact and the weight is `> 0` — the SAME convention as the binary probit (no Fisher-scoring substitution, in contrast to the beta-binomial). The interval probability `Φ(b)−Φ(a)` is computed in whichever tail avoids 1−1 cancellation, reusing the validated tail-stable `_norm_logcdf`/`_norm_pdf` with an explicit `_norm_cdf(±∞)` short-circuit; `φ(±∞)=0` at the end categories. Validated (`test/runtests.jl`, T1): the `K=2, θ=[0]` REDUCTION to `BernoulliProbitResponse` is EXACT for loglik, score, AND observed weight (category 2 ↔ `y=1`, category 1 ↔ `y=0`); on a 3-category family the category probabilities sum to 1, the score is zero-mean (`Σ_k P(k)·score(k)=0`), the score matches a central finite difference of the loglik (rtol 1e-5), the observed weight matches `−(second finite difference)` and is strictly `> 0` (rtol 1e-3); an END-TO-END value gate confirms the ordinal Laplace marginal at `θ=[0]` equals the Bernoulli-probit marginal on the same binary data recoded `1/2` (`laplace_marginal_loglik`, Δ ~1e-16); and strictly-increasing / non-empty threshold plus `1:K` category-range guards throw. A ≥3-category ordinal design is MORE informative than a binary threshold (cf. `V6-PROBIT`), which is the point of the motivating calving-ease trait (T1). JOINT ESTIMATION (doc-20 Step 1): `fit_laplace_reml(...; family = :ordered_probit)` now estimates σ²a AND the `K-1` cutpoints jointly by an IDENTIFIED reparameterization — fix `θ_1 = 0` and estimate `θ_2..θ_{K-1}` via positive increments `θ_j = θ_{j-1} + exp(δ_j)` (strict ordering automatic), K read from the data; the outer NelderMead objective is guarded (a σ²a safety-rail `|log σ²a − log σ²a₀| ≤ 8` + a singular/non-finite penalty) so the weakly-identified small-data MLE cannot run to the boundary. Validated (`test/runtests.jl`, T1 fit): the K=2 fit reduces EXACTLY to `fit_laplace_reml(...; family = :bernoulli_probit)` (σ²a rtol 1e-3, marginal loglik atol 1e-5, `cutpoints == [0]`); the K=3 fit on a structured pedigree returns strictly-ordered cutpoints (`θ_1=0 < θ_2`), a rail-bounded σ²a, a self-consistent marginal loglik at the estimate, and `converged`; guards reject `< 1`/non-integer codes and `marginal = :variational`. SAME-ESTIMAND COMPARATOR RUN (2026-07-01): `ordinal::clmm` (Laplace-ML, probit — glmmTMB does NOT fit cumulative-link ordinal) on an identical A=I / repeated-records K=3 packet (80 animals × 4 records) agrees with the `:ordered_probit` joint fit — cutpoint SPACING Δ 0.004 (essentially exact, after aligning the intercept convention), σ²a Δ 0.024 (ML-vs-REML), intercept Δ 0.012, both converged (`docs/dev-log/recovery-checkpoints/2026-07-01-ordinal-clmm-comparator.md`). PRE-DECLARED 48-SEED RECOVERY GATE PASSED (2026-07-01): known-truth A=I/repeated-records K=3 recovery on an INFORMATIVE design (`sim/phase6_ordinal_recovery.jl`, predeclared `3bef5b03` before the run) — 48/48 converged, `|bias| ≤ 2·MCSE` for σ²a (bias +0.027, 1.44·MCSE — the weak axis), the cutpoint θ_2 (0.58·MCSE), AND β; no detectable bias (`docs/dev-log/recovery-checkpoints/2026-07-01-ordinal-recovery-48seed.md`); the informative design resolves the small-data weak-identification.",
